1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:05,291
Earned Valor brings fitness, adventure, and friendly competition to the living room TV.

2
00:00:05,431 --> 00:00:11,533
Train with a medieval mentor, grow your squire through completed routines, and challenge another fighter.

3
00:00:11,673 --> 00:00:16,622
Our goal is to give families and friends a reason to move, play, and return together.

4
00:00:17,883 --> 00:00:21,863
This video uses a synthetic skeleton instead of a live camera.

5
00:00:21,863 --> 00:00:26,928
The game footage is recorded from the native Android TV app in an emulator.

6
00:00:28,183 --> 00:00:32,192
Chapter One, The First Oath, introduces Sir Alden and Mara.

7
00:00:32,192 --> 00:00:37,804
Explore the courtyard, follow objectives, and choose how your squire responds in the story.

8
00:00:39,083 --> 00:00:44,441
The skeleton on the right sends the same movement landmarks used by the phone controller.

9
00:00:44,441 --> 00:00:48,370
The right hand guides the sword; the left places the shield.

10
00:00:48,370 --> 00:00:50,155
Menus support the TV remote.

11
00:00:51,417 --> 00:00:52,665
Combat rewards timing.

12
00:00:52,665 --> 00:00:58,073
Cover the incoming attack line, watch stamina, and counter when an opening appears.

13
00:00:58,073 --> 00:01:02,233
Health and sword reach determine whether a deliberate sweep lands.

14
00:01:03,483 --> 00:01:06,328
When movement tracking disappears, both fighters wait.

15
00:01:06,328 --> 00:01:12,422
Reacquiring the skeleton resumes the duel without turning the missing interval into an extra strike.

16
00:01:13,683 --> 00:01:18,970
Alden's training hall builds a routine around squat and push up variations.

17
00:01:18,970 --> 00:01:23,816
Each exercise calibrates its starting and lower positions before counting begins.

18
00:01:25,083 --> 00:01:27,227
A partial movement is rejected.

19
00:01:27,227 --> 00:01:31,087
A controlled lower and full return count one repetition.

20
00:01:31,087 --> 00:01:37,947
These are synthetic test poses exercising the real counting rules, rather than measurements of a person.

21
00:01:39,217 --> 00:01:42,794
After the prescribed rest, the next exercise calibrates separately.

22
00:01:42,794 --> 00:01:49,948
This recording shortens the routine and rest, while the app keeps the required sets and full movement cycles.

23
00:01:51,217 --> 00:01:54,889
The completed test circuit appears in this demo profile.

24
00:01:54,889 --> 00:02:01,009
Local squires keep separate story and training saves, with weekly practice goals and bounded progression.

25
00:02:02,283 --> 00:02:05,780
Clan Wars pairs one to three fighters per side.

26
00:02:05,780 --> 00:02:09,278
Here, two scripted skeleton controllers demonstrate the shared match.

27
00:02:09,278 --> 00:02:13,163
The server resolves health, the result, and the clan score.

28
00:02:14,417 --> 00:02:21,649
Today, the prototype supports personal progress and local clan duels, with equal starting gear for competitive matches.

29
00:02:21,789 --> 00:02:29,255
Our vision is online play with family and friends across homes, followed by opt-in matches against new rivals and clans.

30
00:02:29,395 --> 00:02:31,209
Online matchmaking is planned.

31
00:02:31,349 --> 00:02:32,426
Train your body.

32
00:02:32,426 --> 00:02:33,503
Forge your legend.
